<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>ConsentText</key>
	<dict>
		<key>default</key>
		<string>TRAFFIC-ANALYSIS DEFENSE — ENFORCED

This profile configures the TAD VPN VPN and sets a minimum traffic-analysis defense level
of "moderate". You can raise the level in the app. You cannot lower it while this profile
is installed.

WHAT THE DEFENSE DOES

It injects cover traffic and pads packets to a constant size so that an observer watching
the encrypted tunnel cannot infer which sites you visit from packet sizes and timing.

WHAT IT COSTS

Real bandwidth and battery. Cover traffic is indistinguishable from your traffic to an
observer, which means it is also indistinguishable to your data plan. Expect materially
higher data use, more so at "moderate" and "heavy".

FAIL-CLOSED BEHAVIOUR

If the server cannot run the matching server-side defense, the app refuses to connect
rather than leave you believing you are protected when you are not.

LIMITS

- This enforces a floor, not the device. Removing this profile removes the floor.
- The defense protects traffic inside this VPN tunnel. Traffic that does not go through
  the tunnel is not protected.

Removable at: Settings &gt; General &gt; VPN &amp; Device Management (unless your organisation has
supervised this device and disallowed removal).
</string>
	</dict>
	<key>PayloadContent</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>OnDemandEnabled</key>
			<integer>1</integer>
			<key>OnDemandRules</key>
			<array>
				<dict>
					<key>Action</key>
					<string>Connect</string>
				</dict>
			</array>
			<key>PayloadDescription</key>
			<string>Configures the VPN and pins a minimum traffic-analysis defense level.</string>
			<key>PayloadDisplayName</key>
			<string>TAD VPN — defense floor: moderate</string>
			<key>PayloadIdentifier</key>
			<string>com.github.tellebo.ios-configuration-profiles.tad.vpn</string>
			<key>PayloadType</key>
			<string>com.apple.vpn.managed</string>
			<key>PayloadUUID</key>
			<string>9467D9DB-17F3-51FE-B171-6685623614E2</string>
			<key>PayloadVersion</key>
			<integer>1</integer>
			<key>ProviderBundleIdentifier</key>
			<string>com.example.tadvpn.PacketTunnel</string>
			<key>ProviderType</key>
			<string>packet-tunnel</string>
			<key>UserDefinedName</key>
			<string>TAD VPN</string>
			<key>VPNSubType</key>
			<string>com.example.tadvpn</string>
			<key>VPNType</key>
			<string>VPN</string>
			<key>VendorConfig</key>
			<dict>
				<key>TADConstantPacketSize</key>
				<true/>
				<key>TADDefenseLevel</key>
				<string>moderate</string>
				<key>TADEnforced</key>
				<true/>
				<key>TADMaxBlockingFraction</key>
				<string>0.2</string>
				<key>TADMaxPaddingFraction</key>
				<string>0.5</string>
				<key>TADRequirePeerSupport</key>
				<true/>
				<key>TADServerEndpoint</key>
				<string>vpn.example.com:51820</string>
			</dict>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>PayloadDescription</key>
	<string>Pins a minimum traffic-analysis defense level for the TAD VPN app.</string>
	<key>PayloadDisplayName</key>
	<string>Traffic-Analysis Defense — enforced (moderate)</string>
	<key>PayloadIdentifier</key>
	<string>com.github.tellebo.ios-configuration-profiles.tad</string>
	<key>PayloadOrganization</key>
	<string>tellebo/iOS-Configuration-Profiles</string>
	<key>PayloadRemovalDisallowed</key>
	<false/>
	<key>PayloadScope</key>
	<string>System</string>
	<key>PayloadType</key>
	<string>Configuration</string>
	<key>PayloadUUID</key>
	<string>83623FA6-8056-5DB8-BB6E-3CB9E19F0AF6</string>
	<key>PayloadVersion</key>
	<integer>1</integer>
</dict>
</plist>
